DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  macro  ooffffsseettooff()  returns the offset of the field _m_e_m_b_e_r from the
       start of the structure _t_y_p_e.

       This macro is useful because the sizes of the  fields  that  compose  a
       structure  can  vary  across  implementations, and compilers may insert
       different numbers of padding bytes between  fields.   Consequently,  an
       element’s  offset  is  not necessarily given by the sum of the sizes of
       the previous elements.

       A compiler error will result if _m_e_m_b_e_r is not aligned to a byte  bound‐
       ary (i.e., it is a bit field).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       ooffffsseettooff()  returns  the  offset  of  the given _m_e_m_b_e_r within the given
       _t_y_p_e, in units of bytes.

